 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Howe'er the love between\nThe lips of olden generations,\nOh, while young eyes see not again\nThe joy they thrilled with their maiden,\nAnd every star that ever\nBurned up a gleaming tree,\nTheir spark can bring as well as ever,\nThat light beneath her May glory\nIn blossom and clear spring-tide heaven\nIs withered to ashes here. Away!\nAs from its gaudy ruin fallen\nMust Yon Stouffer's faded",
